#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158351} :activity/id #uuid "980e0bea-1189-578f-9781-512b76215027" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048859 :topic/id #uuid "c6e63ba3-f17e-5d7d-8b1e-f7ca5b0feff7" :topic/math-academy-id 2824} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158351 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158568 :tutorial/content "We've seen how to calculate the total derivative of a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R.$ In this lesson, we will learn how to calculate its second derivative.\n\nFor a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n\n![](images/44/44a95860d7e7bd926f4d94c2ebb5b037e8537ac622f7c86b500aa06b9f959250.svg)\n\nthe total derivative of $f$ is given by the matrix\n\n![](images/e0/e0c9f72b67a531f992342e9f9e0b74f447de5e2b62c9fd81f08804096a912e67.svg)\n\nTo differentiate $f$ once more, we first need to take the transpose of the first derivative:\n\n![](images/4d/4d23282171c39149eeebd7301550ebdf1727b86736a57de6e5d7b6ea96891157.svg)\n\nTo calculate the **second derivative** of $f,$ we simply apply the definition of the total derivative to $\\left(\\boldsymbol f'(\\mathbf x)\\right)^T.$ By doing this, we get the following $n\\times n$ matrix:\n\n![](images/3d/3d62db0c4018fcce47077285aa05e6c4ea3c79e972ab87fccf5165a07083eda9.svg)\n\nNotice that this matrix is *symmetric* due to the equality of mixed partial derivatives. This becomes important later. \n\nThe matrix $\\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x)$ is sometimes called the **Hessian matrix,** and its determinant, \n\n$$\nH(\\mathbf x) = \\det\\big( \\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x) \\big)\n$$\n\nis called the **Hessian determinant**.\n\nNote that in the case of a two-variable function $f(x,y),$ the second derivative is given by\n\n![](images/e8/e83195902ce2cdc2e0ff6c1f51ebc679a4bddd51fedd38c4bc6fddc4c73373dd.svg)\n\nIn this lesson, we'll primarily focus on two-variable functions $f(x,y).$ However, we should remember that the techniques discussed here can be applied to scalar functions with an arbitrary number of variables." :tutorial/id #uuid "79cc27de-f461-55d9-ab0f-3dd5a21dd4f4" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7795 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "bac39a49-196c-50bd-99ec-d3c5b74be977" :step/math-academy-id 45105 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158352}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158352 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157000 :question/id #uuid "332b1d25-852f-51ad-9a38-62b562ae247f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12522"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048781} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049696} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049962} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050021}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157540} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157791} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284388} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351224} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389421} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394112} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430444} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430447} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435393} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435394}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"} :step/id #uuid "bdf28805-f615-5f91-bade-c3cb7038cfd2" :step/math-academy-id 45106 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158354}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158353 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157001 :question/id #uuid "53ca572c-798a-5529-9702-df3291a2b500" :question/math-academy-id "e-12523"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049044}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157792} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157793} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235547} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237927} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284389} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284390} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284391} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351196} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430448} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435395}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"} :step/id #uuid "e732cfd5-6c10-55ef-b698-a932a1d233c3" :step/math-academy-id 45109} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158354 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157002 :question/id #uuid "235325ea-4a42-5f63-974a-edd459a4a771" :question/math-academy-id "e-12524"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157541} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157790} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351225} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351229} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351230} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394105} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430445} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430446} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481414}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"} :step/id #uuid "8222059e-dad9-55b4-8e1d-ac327c86df18" :step/math-academy-id 45116 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158353}}] :activity/title "The Second Derivative of a Multivariable Function" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186157481}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481451} :activity/id #uuid "0d220057-0079-57e6-bb5c-eb3461a91e72" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048859 :topic/id #uuid "c6e63ba3-f17e-5d7d-8b1e-f7ca5b0feff7" :topic/math-academy-id 2824} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481442 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62d58fc9-233d-5a98-9f47-8a3790a441f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236443} {:answer/id #uuid "804c671d-3217-5280-aa02-fe2a73812ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236615} {:answer/id #uuid "88c43743-4bdd-5d6d-8482-949f26f0705c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236672} {:answer/id #uuid "944e0f31-80d6-5eac-8960-7ada905bec43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-2{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236758} {:answer/id #uuid "d93bce69-5901-5324-bd97-83116ddf04a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237192}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236672} :answer-field/id #uuid "77c1b5e6-8017-5a27-ad73-0d376c902134" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ba2b3d0e-8f3a-5211-b064-2ffdb4af104d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102688" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(\\pi ,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}],$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) & -{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(\\pi ,-1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(\\pi ,-1)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(\\pi ,-1)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=-1.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "098d6e52-39b3-522b-84c5-e656d2477a6a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481463}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481451 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351196 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a863fee-48cb-518a-94c7-332f0d5dfb90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348671} {:answer/id #uuid "236352e1-e284-5137-93e8-01d0c0b82dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348749} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6da9cd-0b80-5391-a066-ff87ff441cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350254} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b5d5ad-403a-5e9b-b47e-9495ed54eecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350322} {:answer/id #uuid "da828216-6cb2-53d2-9a0c-74a4b4c5a870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350365}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350365} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f56bbbf-1a13-5c6d-a2d7-69c5469daa32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0dab700a-fa4f-5675-9473-37a2b428ee20" :question/math-academy-id "q-81023" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2(x-1){y}^{2} & 2(x-1)^{2}y\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2(x-1){y}^{2} & 2(x-1)^{2}y\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2(x-1){y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2(x-1)^{2}y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=4(x-1)y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=4(x-1)y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=2(x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2} & 4(x-1)y \\\\ 4(x-1)y & 2(x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,1)=2\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-4)=-12.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4e33b2ed-2bc9-51ba-9064-eab461a12ff8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481454}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481454 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93574e00-8aff-52c2-8fef-8d24d76bb02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481016} {:answer/id #uuid "aee9d420-4960-50a5-922a-c43137c76d7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481067} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4a4294-c877-56f6-bfd0-3109ee79c13c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481097} {:answer/id #uuid "c00142a0-9805-5734-8860-3bf5256f853f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481104} {:answer/id #uuid "e631a5f0-8bc9-5fbb-b72c-fddfe67625ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481177}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481177} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cad98c5-f0af-530e-9545-f63d666cd3ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c02d4f47-274a-5db8-9775-386bac66028f" :question/math-academy-id "q-102684" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x} & \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2y\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{y}{x})=-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2y)=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{y}{x})=\\frac{1}{x}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2y)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,2).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,2)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "63ea7e02-9f7a-5a09-b718-d06795e4cb97" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481442}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481455 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fca28ad-f59e-5a0a-bb4c-0662386d1e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480829} {:answer/id #uuid "3075a971-db98-5b66-a3d1-9af12fdf7be7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480831} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb3995c-cc62-5136-82b2-472b0cb824be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481006} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ef3863-4e52-56dd-9984-66598e15e8ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481130} {:answer/id #uuid "dc10b03f-56c5-527c-94f1-47709864755a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481155}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481006} :answer-field/id #uuid "28c26c69-61cb-5d08-9210-43f100a3d7fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cd7463fc-6818-5da6-ab8a-b593c73ec670" :question/math-academy-id "q-102699" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(1,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)=xy-{x}^{2}{y}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-{x}^{2}{y}^{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-{x}^{2}{y}^{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}y-2x{y}^{3} & x-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-2x{y}^{3})=-2{y}^{3}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=1-6x{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-2x{y}^{3})=1-6x{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=-6{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{y}^{3} & 1-6x{y}^{2} \\\\ 1-6x{y}^{2} & -6{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,0).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "66302a80-8659-5359-be45-331fa2372867"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481463 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b6147f2-99cb-5e0e-bfe7-1ab9fcb4bfaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430425} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd5f2d0-f063-5f9a-8554-0e38b366ddee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430426} {:answer/id #uuid "4c3b39c3-ebcc-501e-bf32-f62c8ab6fbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430428} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8b4808-0307-5f43-b835-eaa5d7c78ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430432} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d3bd0b-8f50-5fda-8e7a-df552a252f05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430436}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430425} :answer-field/id #uuid "57597420-75c9-5305-b6c7-82cc31ede092" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f2460b1b-0ae3-5791-81e8-e644fac55aa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-102692" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} & 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} & 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=\\frac{2y}{x}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{2y}{x} & 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=(-1)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 2=-4.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a882a718-46ae-5afd-bb1b-85e1be5639e2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481455}}] :activity/title "The Second Derivative of a Multivariable Function" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480731}]}
